• If we need a new resources that is not present in k8s cluster, we can do it by extending the capabilities of API and adding it to K8s Cluster. 


• Main objects are - 

	1. Custom Resource Defination - It is a definition file/ template  that has all the fields that a resources should have, How a resources should be validated 

	2. Custom Resource - It is the running instance of CRD. It extends the K8s API. It is an extension of the Kubernetes API that is not necessarily available in a default Kubernetes installation.

	3. Custom Resource Controller- Manages / Monitors the lifecycle of CR. Like we have deployment controller for deployment, node controller for node. 

Once we create the Custom Resource, K8s does the  validation of the  the resources through CRD.

• CustomCrontroller is written in Golang

• Flow - 

DevOPS creates the CRD 
users / Developer create the CR 
K8s does the validation of the resource using CRD
DevOPS also creates Custom controller that manages / monitors the lifecycle of the CR and ensures the destired state is maintained. 



Link - https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/extend-kubernetes/custom-resources/custom-resource-definitions/ 
Custom Resource - 
---
apiVersion: apiextensions.k8s.io/v1
kind: CustomResourceDefinition
metadata:
  name: internals.datasets.kodekloud.com  
spec:
  group: datasets.kodekloud.com
  versions:
    - name: v1
      served: true
      storage: true
      schema:
        openAPIV3Schema:
          type: object
          properties:
            spec:
              type: object
              properties:
                internalLoad:
                  type: string
                range:
                  type: integer
                percentage:
                  type: string
  scope: Namespaced
  names:
    plural: internals
    singular: internal
    kind: Internal
    shortNames:
    - int    Scenerio 2- Create CR from existing CRD -   Create CR - 
